  "rawText": "Unit Six : Leisure 59\nDiscuss in pairs and answer this question orally.\nWhich activities mainly take place in cities and which activities mainly take\nplace in villages? Also say which activity or activities can take place both\nin cities and villages.\nWork in groups. Here is a list of children’s activities. Which of them are\nfree-time or leisure activities and which are not? Why are they so?\n© studying for exams\ne listening to music\n¢ visiting relatives on weekends\n¢ attending music lessons\nreading story books\n® going to movies\nhelping parents with housework\n¢ going on a picnic with family or friends\ne walking in the park on holidays\nWrite answers to these questions.\n1, What free-time / leisure activities do you do?\n2, Where and with whom do you do your Icisure activitics?\n3, Why do you like or dislike to do your free-time activitics?\n4, Do you face any problems or difficulties in doing your leisure activities?\nLesson 4: Travelling by train (1)\nAsk and answer these questions.\n1, Have you ever travelled by train?\n2, If you have, when, where, with whom, and why did you go?\nListen to the teacher /audio and answer the following questions.\nListening text: 7\nTick the best answer.\n1, The school is closed for\na. winter.\nb. summer.\nc. autumn.",
